      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure it\u0027s that helpful. For `MutexProtected` we do this to make holding the mutex type safe - `Use()` iirc passes a noncopyable nonmovable handle into the function. But here, `Promote()` returns a `Ref\u003cT\u003e` which safe because even if it does escape the scope, it still holds the ref. `Use()` seems the same except it gets us a `T*` instead.\n\nSo a pattern like this seems fine:\n\n```cpp\nif (auto /*Ref\u003cQueueBase\u003e*/ q \u003d queue.Promote()) {\n  return q-\u003eGetCompletedCommandSerial();\n} else {\n  return completionSerial;\n}\n```",
      "revId": "c707a19fcdb1738645c66c819636d48c04ff88da",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b085d458_44d80afb",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
